{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>The wise man.</b> He compared the wise man to one who sees, who has eyes in his head, so that he goes wherever he wishes and sees the straight path and the crooked one. But the fool — in darkness he walks; he does not know what he stumbles over. \"And this I knew,\" and also I knew that one fate befalls them all."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:04.529253480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}